  "id": "Compound::DB01144 - Gene::766",
  "verbalization": "Diclofenamide is implicated in a complex network of interactions that ultimately connect it to Ca7 through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Diclofenamide binds to Ca14 or Ca5b, both of which participate in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, an activity that is also associated with Ca7. This implies a potential role for Diclofenamide in influencing the activity of Ca7 through these shared pathways. Additionally, the involvement of Ca14 in carbonate dehydratase activity further supports a link between Diclofenamide and Ca7, highlighting a possible mechanism by which the drug may modulate the function of this calcium-related entity. The integrated evidence suggests a plausible, though indirect, relationship between Diclofenamide and Ca7, mediated through the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide and related enzymatic activities.",
